00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:32.960
<v Mike>It was on the Atari ST and the Amiga and stuff like that.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:38.220
<v Mike>Uh, so I think the NES version was made by a group called Gremlin Graphics, which doesn't

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.760
<v Mike>sound, uh, real, but sure.

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:44.920
<v Sean>What's the Gremlin Graph? The magnetic fields.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.080
<v Mike>Oh, Electrobrain.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:49.040
<v Mike>Right. You're right. Published, published by Electrobrain.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.300
<v Mike>Oh, okay. So there we go.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:56.360
<v Mike>Um, and there's a lot of things to talk about with the computer version.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:00.900
<v Mike>Uh, there's a lot to break down in terms of the similarities between the NES version and

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.600
<v Mike>the changes in the computer version and everything.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:07.380
<v Mike>But I think we could save that maybe for the end and focus on the NES version because

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:14.100
<v Mike>this NES version, while mostly the same, uh, you know, the, the, the core loop of the game

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:19.240
