<v Mike>The, uh, the progression all happens in this, uh, screen where you're at like a car dealership,

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:33.560
<v Mike>where there's a, uh, parts section and a buy cars section, just like in real dealerships,

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:37.400
<v Mike>uh, where you go get your car serviced, but it turns out you also bought your car there,

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:41.380
<v Joe>but you'll never step back in that room again, unless you want to buy another car.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.680
<v Mike>Like they keep themselves, uh, separated.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:44.760
<v Mike>It's like, oh, that's weird.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.020
<v Mike>I'll never see the guy who sold me my car again.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.680
<v Mike>Anyway, uh, the shop.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:53.680
<v Sean>Did you have like a traumatic experience at the, at the car dealership?

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.200
<v Mike>Maybe. Right.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.440
<v Mike>Maybe I liked that guy.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.440
<v Mike>Maybe I thought I was going to see him again in my life.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:05.900
<v Mike>And so between the races, you visit the garage to repair damage to the car, uh, you know,

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:09.000
<v Mike>refuel, re-air the tires, fix the engine.

